  "rationale": "With no defences deployed, every 'NOT patched/segmented/mfa' condition holds. The shortest path is: (1) phish_workstation, which gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user; (2) pivot_internal, which gives reach_internal; (3) auth_ciserver, which gives foothold_ciserver; (4) escalate_ciserver, which gives admin_ciserver; (5) leak_secrets_ciserver, which gives stolen_dbadmin; (6) auth_db, which gives foothold_db; (7) escalate_db, which gives admin_db; (8) exfiltrate_db, which gives exfiltrated. Every exfiltration step needs an admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup, which needs a foothold on that host, and that foothold needs both reach_internal and stolen_dbadmin. The CI-server leak is the cheapest way to get stolen_dbadmin, at 4 steps after the pivot chain begins. The DC or ADFS route needs kerberoasting plus auth, escalate and dump, which takes 10 steps in total. So the minimum is 8 techniques."
